Subject: [PATCH] nvme-pci: restore config space if the device resets again after FLR

A controller can lose its PCI config space again shortly after the FLR
fallback has restored it, either because the FLR completes
asynchronously after pcie_flr()'s pci_dev_wait() saw config space start
responding, or because the firmware begins its own internal reset.  The
function still answers config reads, but it is back at power-on
defaults: PCI_COMMAND reads 0 and the BARs are unassigned, so the
register window decodes nothing and every MMIO read returns ~0.  The
next reset then fails at the CSTS check in nvme_pci_enable() with
-ENODEV, which nvme_reset_work() turns into a dead controller with no
retry, so the drive needs a power cycle after all.

The driver cannot recover from this today for two reasons.  Nothing
restores the config space a second time, as pci_enable_resources() only
ORs the command bits and never rewrites BARs.  And pci_restore_state()
ends with "dev->state_saved = false", so any further restore is a silent
no-op; nvme_pci_enable() does re-arm the saved copy with
pci_save_state(), but that call sits after the CSTS check and the
failing path never reaches it.

Fix both halves.  Re-arm the saved copy right after the FLR restore in
nvme_dev_disable(), where dev->saved_config_space still holds the
known-good copy we just wrote, and make nvme_pci_enable() restore it
once more and retry the CSTS read before declaring the device gone.  A
genuinely absent device still fails the second read and returns -ENODEV
as before, so no reset is prolonged.

---
diff -Nur a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/pci.c
@@ -2674,8 +2674,20 @@
 	pci_set_master(pdev);
 
 	if (readl(dev->bar + NVME_REG_CSTS) == -1) {
-		result = -ENODEV;
-		goto disable;
+		/*
+		 * A device that finishes an internal reset after its config
+		 * space was restored comes back with default BARs and command
+		 * register, so its register window decodes nothing and every
+		 * read returns ~0. Restore the config space once more and
+		 * retry before declaring the device gone.
+		 */
+		pci_restore_state(pdev);
+		if (readl(dev->bar + NVME_REG_CSTS) == -1) {
+			result = -ENODEV;
+			goto disable;
+		}
+		dev_info(dev->ctrl.device,
+			 "config space restored after late device reset\n");
 	}
 
 	/*
@@ -2806,6 +2818,14 @@
 					 result);
 			} else {
 				pci_restore_state(pdev);
+				/*
+				 * pci_restore_state() clears state_saved, but
+				 * the device can lose its config space again
+				 * if it completes an internal reset after this
+				 * point. Re-arm the saved copy so the reset
+				 * path can restore it once more.
+				 */
+				pci_save_state(pdev);
 				dev_info(dev->ctrl.device,
 					 "controller %s completed after pcie flr\n",
 					 shutdown ? "shutdown" : "disable");
-- 
2.34.1
